      "ownershipVehicle": "UGI Utilities, Inc.",
      "description": "UGI Utilities – Electric Division is a regulated electric transmission, distribution and retail utility serving more than 63,000 customers in Luzerne and Wyoming counties in northeastern Pennsylvania. The business operates approximately 2,700 miles of transmission and distribution lines and 14 substations. UGI Utilities, Inc., a wholly owned subsidiary of UGI Corporation, remains the current legal owner. Funds managed by Argo Infrastructure Partners LP signed an approximately $470 million definitive purchase agreement on April 28, 2026, but UGI's August 2026 Form 10-Q continued to classify the business as held for sale and expected closing in UGI fiscal Q2 2027, subject to customary closing conditions and applicable regulatory approvals. The exact Argo fund, manager-level stake, standalone legal suffix, headquarters, founding year and separate website are not publicly disclosed. Wyoming Valley Electric Holdings LLC and related acquisition entities are transaction vehicles for this same target, not separate PortCos. No legal close, termination, resale or revised timetable was identified through August 16, 2026.",
